#: templates/admin/modules/mailer.php:473
msgid "Why: Auto-Submitted: auto-generated stops auto-replies and out-of-office replies from looping. Bulk mail such as newsletters also gets Precedence: bulk, which tells receivers it is not a one-to-one message."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/modules/mailer.php:514
msgid "Why: a valid DKIM signature is one of the strongest trust signals for spam filters, and it is required for DMARC alignment. Signing only happens when the From address belongs to the DKIM domain."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/modules/mailer.php:459
msgid "Why: every mail gets a unique, domain-aligned Message-ID, so providers can thread it, deduplicate it, and trace bounces back to this site."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/modules/mailer.php:466
msgid "Why: identifies the sending software (TrayDigita Core Mailer) in the headers, which helps postmasters and support diagnose delivery problems."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/modules/mailer.php:480
msgid "Why: lets the site owner track spam complaints per list in the provider dashboard, so a bad list can be found and fixed instead of hurting the whole domain."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/modules/mailer.php:452
msgid "Why: mailbox providers show an unsubscribe button instead of a spam button, and Gmail requires a one-click unsubscribe header for bulk senders. The link points to the From address by email, plus the site’s unsubscribe page when a module provides one."
msgstr ""

#: templates/admin/modules/mailer.php:445
msgid "Why: replies go to the site’s From address instead of bouncing from a no-reply address, and a matching Reply-To is a trust signal for spam filters."
msgstr ""

